<!-- CONFIDENCE COACHING -->
<div class="offer-block" id="confidence-coaching">
<div class="offer-header">
<span class="offer-tag">Confidence Coaching</span>
<h2>Two sessions to change how you carry yourself under attention.</h2>
<p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.05rem;">Not a script for your next talk. A reset in how you relate to being watched. What you put into the gap between sessions decides what you get out of it.</p>
</div>
<div class="pricing-grid">
<div class="pricing-card">
<h4>Solo</h4>
<div class="price">NZD $300</div>
<div class="price-unit">two 1-hour sessions</div>
<p>Full personalisation, one on one. Includes a short paid diagnostic ($50, credited toward booking) before we start, so we're working from what's actually driving the fear, not guessing. It's rarely the content.</p>
</div>
<div class="pricing-card featured">
<h4>Group of Four</h4>
<div class="price">NZD $120</div>
<div class="price-unit">per person, two 1-hour sessions</div>
<p>Same format, three other people in the room, because a live audience is the actual thing you're afraid of, not a concept. Watching three others go through the same recalibration shows you the fear from the outside first.</p>
</div>
<div class="pricing-card">
<h4>Add-ons</h4>
<div class="price" style="font-size: 1.2rem;">NZD $40 / $90</div>
<div class="price-unit">gap check-in / critique</div>
<p><strong>Gap Check-In ($40):</strong> a short note between sessions so the second session starts from where you actually are.<br/><br/><strong>Presentation Critique ($90/hr, core clients only):</strong> once the foundational work is done, a fast, specific critique on one talk for one room.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="pricing-note">
<strong>What to expect:</strong> this works if you do the practice between sessions. I bring the diagnostic and the method; the gap between sessions is yours. Two sessions won't undo what two sessions of effort can't reach.
      </div>
